  "file": "formulas/operator-precedence.xlsx",
  "kind": "xlsx",
  "proves": "Excel's operator precedence is not the mathematical one. `=-2^2` is 4 because unary minus binds tighter than `^`, and `=2^3^2` is 64 because `^` is left-associative. An engine that reads these the mathematical way produces no error - it silently writes a different number into the user's file on the next recalculation.",
  "valuesVerifiedBy": "LibreOffice 26.2.4.2 0229ac93fcf0d7cbc6376066c6f35021cef002dc recalculation of formulas written without cached values",
